etabolic panel.\n\n2. Atrial Fibrillation.\n• Medical Reasoning: The patient is currently in a good rate.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient on the importance of avoiding foods high in sugar.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 25 mg twice a day.\n\n3. Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease.\n• Medical Reasoning: The patient is currently on protonix 40 mg once a day.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient on the importance of avoiding foods high in sugar.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue protonix 40 mg once a day.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nThe patient will follow up with me in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nHigh blood sugar.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nHannah Davis is a 52-year-old female who presents for evaluation of high blood sugar.\n\nThe patient reports that she has been eating a lot of sweets lately due to the holidays. She felt fine initially but started to feel light headed and was seeing spots after a couple of weeks. She went to the emergency room where she was diagnosed with a high blood sugar. She has been feeling well now.\n\nThe patient reports that she has been doing well with her reflux. She has been taking the protonix 40 mg once a day.\n\nShe has a history of osteoarthritis, atrial fibrillation, and reflux. She is currently taking metoprolol 25 mg twice a day.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Constitutional: Denies fever or chills.\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or shortness of breath.\n• Respiratory: Denies abdominal pain or burning with urination.\n• Musculoskeletal: Denies joint pain or muscle aches.\n• Neurological: Denies headaches.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n• Neck\n\t- General Examination: Thyroid is enlarged but non-tender.\n\t- Carotid: No carotid bruits.\n• Respiratory\n\t- Auscultation of Lungs: Clear.\n• Cardiovascular\n\t- Auscultation of Heart: Irregular rate and 